---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const faqs = [
  ['How much do Docyt, Digits and Truewind cost?', 'Docyt prices per property by quote only (no public price on docyt.com/pricing as of 25 Oct 2026), with unlimited users. Digits bills per client: Essentials $65/mo, Core $100/mo, and Pro $250/mo (listed as coming soon on digits.com/pricing in Oct 2026), with no seat fees. Truewind does not publish pricing; it quotes after a call based on close complexity and volume.'],
  ['Do I have to switch ledgers?', 'Docyt and Digits each run their own ledger: Docyt migrates from QuickBooks, NetSuite, Sage Intacct and others, and Digits is a US-only general ledger fed by bank feeds or CSV. Truewind works alongside your existing systems.'],
  ['Which fits multi-location clients?', 'Docyt. It is built for hotel, restaurant, retail and franchise operators, posts PMS and POS revenue nightly, and prices per property with portfolio discounts as property count grows.'],
  ['Which suits a firm with many small clients?', 'Digits. It prices each client separately with mixed plans, gives the firm unlimited seats, and partner firms keep their own books free.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="Docyt vs Digits vs Truewind for bookkeeping firms — AI close compared"
  description="Docyt, Digits and Truewind side by side for accounting practices: published pricing, who each is built for, and which one fits your client base."
>
  <h1>Docyt vs Digits vs Truewind</h1>
  <p>All three pitch an AI-driven month-end close. They differ most in who they are built for: Docyt for multi-location hospitality and retail, Digits as an AI-native ledger priced per client, Truewind as a close platform for growth-stage finance teams.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/docyt`}>Docyt</a></th><th><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/digits`}>Digits</a></th><th><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/truewind`}>Truewind</a></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Firms with hotel, restaurant, retail or franchise clients that run many locations</td><td>Firms with US small-business and startup clients willing to move to a new ledger</td><td>Firms and in-house teams that want a controlled, reviewer-led close workflow</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</td><td>Per property, quote-only (no public price); unlimited users; annual plans</td><td>Per client: Essentials $65/mo, Core $100/mo, Pro $250/mo; firm's own books free for partner firms; no seat fees</td><td>Not published; quoted after a call based on close complexity and volume</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ledger</td><td>Its own AI-native ERP; migrates from QuickBooks, NetSuite, Sage Intacct and others</td><td>Its own general ledger (US entities only); imports via bank feeds or CSV</td><td>Works alongside your existing systems with integration setup during implementation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Core AI job</td><td>Nightly PMS/POS revenue posting, continuous bank and card reconciliation, closing agent</td><td>24/7 categorization and reconciliation, automated schedules, quality checks, Agentic Close across clients</td><td>Categorization, close execution with reviewer routing, exception handling and audit trail</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Firm angle</td><td>Per-property meter; portfolio pricing drops with property count</td><td>Per-client billing with mixed plans, unlimited firm seats, certification and partner directory</td><td>Implementation-first onboarding; pricing by workflow depth</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>When to choose Docyt</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your clients are multi-location operators (hotels, restaurants, retail) with PMS or POS revenue to post nightly.</li>
    <li>You want a published per-property price and unlimited users.</li>
    <li>You need to catch up months of unreconciled books quickly.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to choose Digits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Clients are US small businesses or startups and can move off QuickBooks or Xero.</li>
    <li>You want to price each client separately and avoid per-seat fees for your team.</li>
    <li>You want to trial the platform on your own firm's books before onboarding clients.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to choose Truewind</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You want close execution with reviewer sign-off and an audit trail more than a new ledger.</li>
    <li>You are fine with a sales call and an implementation project before going live.</li>
    <li>Your close is complex enough that a quoted, workflow-based price makes sense.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/category/month-end-close`}>All month-end close tools</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
